<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <RootNamespace>SafeWebCore.FraudDetection</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- NuGet Package Metadata -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>SafeWebCore.FraudDetection</PackageId>
    <Version>1.1.0</Version>
    <Authors>MPCoreDeveloper</Authors>
    <Company>Posseth Software</Company>
    <Product>SafeWebCore.FraudDetection</Product>
    <Description>
      Optional advanced fraud-detection module for SafeWebCore.
      Detects Western-identity impersonation and penetration-test scanner traffic
      using IP, timezone, language, fingerprint, header, and behavioral signals.
      Supports options pattern configuration with runtime fallback to database-backed settings.
    </Description>
    <PackageTags>fraud;detection;security;scanner;pentest;aspnetcore;safeweb</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/MPCoreDeveloper/SafeWebCore</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/MPCoreDeveloper/SafeWebCore</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
## v1.1.0 — Fail-closed verdicts, per-sink event isolation, added RiskLevel.Unclassified

**Hardening (the API surface stays additive):**
- An unrecognized verdict now maps to `RiskLevel.Unclassified` (appended, `= 4`) instead of `Low`, and the shared verdict-to-action mapping maps it to `RecommendedAction.BlockRequest` instead of `NoAction` — an unknown verdict is never reported as safe
- `FraudEventDispatcher` isolates a throwing `IFraudEventSink` per sink instead of letting it end delivery for every sink registered after it, and counts the swallowed failure in `SafeWebCoreFraudMetrics.FraudEventSinkFailures`

**Also new:**
- `SafeWebCore.FraudDetection` moves to the three-part version `1.1.0` (the four-part `1.0.0.0` normalizes to the already-published `1.0.0`)
- Packaging parity with core: `icon.png`, a `.snupkg` symbol package with SourceLink, and these release notes in the nuspec

**Compatibility:** 100% backward compatible on the public surface — everything new is additive. One intentional tightening: a consumer `switch` over `RiskLevel` without a default arm needs an arm for `Unclassified`.

See CHANGELOG.md and docs/ for full details.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- SourceLink for deterministic builds (parity with SafeWebCore) -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Public API surface tracking for backward compatibility (additive, build-time only) -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers" Version="5.6.0" PrivateAssets="All" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Explicitly register the baseline files so the analyzer picks them up reliably.
       The test project is the only friend assembly, matching the pattern the other packages use. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <AdditionalFiles Include="PublicAPI.Shipped.txt" />
    <AdditionalFiles Include="PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="SafeWebCore.FraudDetection.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Public API baseline enforcement (roadmap v1.4 item 1.2) -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <GeneratePublicApiFiles>true</GeneratePublicApiFiles>
    <!-- RS0037 = removal or rename of a symbol listed in PublicAPI.Shipped.txt is a hard error.
         This is the primary safeguard for 100% backward compatibility. -->
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);RS0037</WarningsAsErrors>
    <!-- During initial rollout of public API tracking (v1.4 item 1.2):
         - RS0016 (public symbol not declared in the txt files) → warning
         - RS0017 (symbol listed in txt files but not found / not public) → warning
         This lets us introduce the mechanism without a perfect baseline on day one.
         After the baseline is curated and stable, remove these from WarningsNotAsErrors / NoWarn
         to enforce a clean public surface. -->
    <WarningsNotAsErrors>$(WarningsNotAsErrors);RS0016;RS0017</WarningsNotAsErrors>
    <!-- RS0027 = we intentionally keep overloads with optional parameters for backward compatibility. -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);RS0027</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\icon.png" Link="icon.png">
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
      <Pack>true</Pack>
    </None>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
